# Scammers and organizations

A scammer is a person (`App\Models\Scammer`). An organization is a company (`App\Models\Organization`). Both store `name` (max 100 characters), `profile_picture_path`, and `is_active`, and both use soft deletes.

They link through the `scammers_organizations` pivot. A scammer can belong to many organizations, and an organization can have many scammers. A report does not require the other side.

## Which side the report names

- A scammer report uses `StoreScammerReportRequest`. `scammer.name` is required. `organizations` is optional.
- An organization report uses `StoreOrganizationReportRequest`. `organization.name` is required. `scammers` is optional.
- The report still needs at least one contact or payment method on that primary subject. A linked organization or scammer does not satisfy that check. See `reports.mdc`.
- A report filed against an existing scammer or organization by id does not send contacts or payment methods. See `reports.mdc`.

## Attaching the other side later

- Scammer to organization: `StoreScammerOrganizationRequest`.
- Organization to scammer: `StoreOrganizationScammerRequest`.

`name` is required. `profile_picture_path`, `contacts`, and `payment_methods` are optional. `contacts.*.platform` and `payment_methods.*.type` are prohibited. Infer the platform with `PlatformType::fromReference` and the payment type with `PaymentMethodType::fromReference`.

## Pivots

Do not attach these from a controller. The scammer and organization repositories own the writes.

- Scammer: `scammers_contacts`, `scammers_payment_methods`, `scammers_reports`, `scammers_organizations`.
- Organization: `organizations_contacts`, `organizations_payment_methods`, `organizations_reports`, and the same `scammers_organizations` pivot.

Deleting a scammer or organization soft-deletes its contact, payment-method, and report pivot rows. Restoring the model restores those rows.
